# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Local dev uses a dedicated PG14 cluster on port 5433.
#
# App runtime: connect as a NON-privileged role so RLS is enforced (ADR-0002).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://ai_hr_app@127.0.0.1:5433/ai_hr_dev
# Application connections per process (1–40, default10). Budget across all replicas.
# AIHR_DB_POOL_MAX=10
# Migrations/admin: the owner role.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:5433/ai_hr_dev
# Tests.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://ai_hr_app@127.0.0.1:5433/ai_hr_test
TEST_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:5433/ai_hr_test

# Demo identity (seeded by `pnpm db:seed`) — isolated development/demo data only.
# Customer sign-in is implemented as embedded HR login, MFA and recovery (AUTH_PROVIDER=internal).
# Follow deploy/internal-auth/README.md and deploy/.env.customer.example for installation settings;
# this development template does not activate or verify customer authentication.
DEV_TENANT_ID=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
DEV_USER_ID=22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

# Public origin for the shared password and demo switcher (no AUTH_PROVIDER) and for local development.
# The own-leave Assistant review checks the browser's Origin against this value and refuses every request
# without it; email and letter links use it too. An origin only: no path, query, credentials or trailing
# text. HTTPS in production. http://localhost:<port> or http://127.0.0.1:<port> is accepted only outside a
# production build. AUTH_PROVIDER=internal or keycloak reads the same variable under its own stricter
# rules (HTTPS always). An invalid value is refused, never replaced by NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI.
# AUTH_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Legacy WorkOS adapter only: these JWT settings are not required by embedded HR authentication.
# For an explicitly configured legacy installation, use its exact issuer, never an incoming token.
# AuthKit issuer without a custom Auth API domain:
# WORKOS_JWT_ISSUER=https://api.workos.com/
# Set an audience only when the configured JWT contract publishes one (AuthKit does not by default).
# WORKOS_JWT_AUDIENCE=

# AI gateway (ADR-0007 / ADR-0023) — OPTIONAL. Shared by the Assistant and embedded AI features.
# AI proposes drafts and answers from authorized reads; a person confirms consequential effects.
# Without a provider, AI drafting is unavailable; manual HR workflows still run without a key.
#
# Per-tenant config is set in-app at /control-tower/agents/provider (provider + model + API key, encrypted at rest). The
# vars below are the PLATFORM fallback used when a tenant has not configured its own provider.
#
# AI_CONFIG_SECRET — REQUIRED to store tenant keys in-app. Master passphrase (>=16 chars) that
# AES-256-GCM-encrypts keys at rest (tenant id as AAD). Without it, in-app key storage is disabled
# (the env keys below still work). Rotating it makes existing stored keys unrecoverable — re-enter them.
# AI_CONFIG_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Optional device-key enrollment pilot. Unset/empty keeps enrollment disabled; never EXPO_PUBLIC.
# Deployment-owned versioned tenant/company/actor/platform allowlist; see ADR-0147 before enabling.
# AIHR_MOBILE_ENROLLMENT_POLICY=
# Signed online clocking has a separate default-disabled rollout; enrollment never enables it.
# AIHR_MOBILE_CLOCK_POLICY=
# Server-only Google service-account JSON for Play Integrity. Never use EXPO_PUBLIC_ for this value.
# Missing/invalid credentials disable fresh Android signed clocking; no fallback credential lookup.
# AIHR_MOBILE_GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
# Offline clocking has its own default-disabled rollout (docs/research/mobile-offline-attendance-protocol.md,
# "Deployment configuration and assembly"). Unset/empty keeps it off; malformed fails closed. Each listed actor must
# ALSO be in AIHR_MOBILE_CLOCK_POLICY for the platform, which owns apiOrigin, app target and Play settings. Owner
# limits 2026-10-28: windowMs 24 h (schema cap 72 h), permitCount 8, maximumIssuesPerHour 4, photoRetentionMs 30 days
# (to be confirmed with counsel before real data). mode "drain" keeps upload/close and refuses new issuance.
# Keyless (owner decision D16, 29 October 2026): no signing key, issuer registry or KMS. The server accepts a claim only
# against its own recorded context and the phone's hardware key. The former "signingKeyId"/"issuers" fields and the
# AIHR_MOBILE_OFFLINE_SIGNING_KEY variable are gone; a policy still carrying them fails closed. AI_CONFIG_SECRET (already
# required) stores claims and photos encrypted. Placeholders only, one line:
# AIHR_MOBILE_OFFLINE_POLICY={"version":1,"mode":"active","windowMs":86400000,"permitCount":8,"maximumIssuesPerHour":4,"photoRetentionMs":2592000000,"entries":[{"tenantId":"<uuid>","companyId":"<uuid>","actorIds":["<app-user-uuid>"]}]}
# Native push (M10, D6): read only by scripts/mobile-push-sweep.ts and the push status endpoint (lib/mobile-push-config.ts).
# A provider whose variables are absent or unusable is OFF (the sweep logs a no-op). Server-only; never EXPO_PUBLIC_.
# APNs token auth: the .p8 key's Key ID and the Team ID (10 characters each), the .p8 PEM (literal \n read as newlines),
# the iOS bundle id (apns-topic), and production|development matching the builds' aps-environment (default production;
# a mismatch makes APNs answer BadDeviceToken, which revokes registrations).
# AIHR_PUSH_APNS_KEY_ID=
# AIHR_PUSH_APNS_TEAM_ID=
# AIHR_PUSH_APNS_PRIVATE_KEY=
# AIHR_PUSH_APNS_BUNDLE_ID=
# AIHR_PUSH_APNS_ENVIRONMENT=production
# Optional private file (0600) in which successive sweep runs reuse the APNs provider token (Apple: refresh 20-60 min).
# AIHR_PUSH_APNS_TOKEN_CACHE=
# FCM HTTP v1: the Firebase project id and that project's service-account JSON on one line (FCM send permission).
# AIHR_PUSH_FCM_PROJECT_ID=
# AIHR_PUSH_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
#
# Platform fallback provider keys — any one enables drafting tenant-wide without in-app config:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...                # or GEMINI_API_KEY (Gemini Developer API)
# AI_DRAFT_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8    # optional: override the Anthropic env-fallback model

# ── Payroll feature gates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Multi-cycle payroll (ADR-0024) + typed pay-components (ADR-0025). Both are GATED OFF by default and
# proven byte-identical to the legacy path by their compat tests. Enable AFTER the §7 accountant sign-off
# (owner-authorised 2026-06-20 against YiWei Law's statutory deck — see docs/adr/0024 §7). Set both to
# 'true' for the Chin Hin deployment.
#
# TRACKED BY THE PARITY RATCHET (ADR-0077 slice 1). These two lines are ACTIVE, so this installation
# ships both features on — `LEGACY_ENABLED_MODULE_CODES` in packs/catalog.ts therefore backfills ACTIVE
# `multi_cycle_payroll` / `typed_pay_components` entitlements, and slice 3's move from these env vars to
# the entitlement resolver is a no-op. test/module-catalog-drift.test.ts READS THIS FILE and fails if the
# two stop agreeing in either direction, so commenting a line out here without also removing the code
# from the parity set is a red suite rather than a silent downgrade on the next deploy.
MULTI_CYCLE_PAYROLL_ENABLED=true
TYPED_PAY_COMPONENTS_ENABLED=true
# Payroll Reset (a03b2d9b / 9bc442bc) — lets an ADMIN revert a PROCESSED run back to Draft (payslips
# cleared, loan/claim side-effects reversed, one audited payroll-batch.reset event) and reprocess a
# selected subset of employees as a same-month adjustment run. Processed-only + admin-only; a Closed run
# stays permanently immutable (0011 triggers). Enabled here so the correction workflow is available.
#
# Also parity-tracked: this flag, PAYROLL_UNLOCK_ENABLED below and INDIVIDUAL_TXN_PAY_ENABLED (set on the
# server by deploy/enable-demo-flags.sh) are `LEGACY_ENABLED_SETTINGS` in packs/catalog.ts, backfilled as
# `tenant_setting` rows by migration 0313. Every setting_definition default is `false`, so without those
# rows slice 3 would switch all three OFF for existing tenants. Same read-this-file ratchet as above.
PAYROLL_RESET_ENABLED=true
# Unlock Closed run (9bc442bc) — lets an authorised user (payroll.unlock permission; super_admin by
# default) reopen a CLOSED run back to Processed for correction. High-risk: it reverses the 0011 closed-
# immutability freeze via a transaction-local escape hatch, reopens the pay period, requires a step-up
# confirmation code (OTP) + a reason, and warns if payment was disbursed or statutory returns were filed.
# Every unlock is captured in payroll_status_history + a payroll-batch.unlocked event.
PAYROLL_UNLOCK_ENABLED=true
# Individual (one-off) transaction pay (f1564110 Phase 3, amends ADR-0056) — the payroll kernel PAYS/
# DEDUCTS the Payroll -> Transactions -> Individual ledger at generation: earning/deduction rows fold with
# their picked pay item's statutory flags (componentless legacy rows use conservative defaults - earning =
# EPF/SOCSO/PCB-liable wages, deduction = post-statutory), overtime adds to the OT figure (otSource
# 'individual-txn'), unpaid adds to the unpaid deduction; leave stays record-only. OFF (the default) keeps
# the ledger record-only and payroll byte-identical (guarded by the inert test). Requires
# TYPED_PAY_COMPONENTS_ENABLED for payable rows (fails closed otherwise); with the flag on, new
# earning/deduction entries must name a pay item from the master.
# INDIVIDUAL_TXN_PAY_ENABLED=true
# Group-coordinated cross-employer PCB (ADR-0029) — overrides each employment's filed MTD with the
# combined-month allocation. Leave OFF until a PARALLEL RUN reconciles a real Chin Hin month against the
# current system; the scope-out (designated paymaster) is the safe default until then.
GROUP_PCB_COORDINATION_ENABLED=false
# Audit-log tamper-evidence hash chain (ADR-0030 Layer 2). OFF by default leaves the domain_event chain
# columns NULL (byte-identical). When 'true', a BEFORE INSERT trigger chains every new event per tenant;
# verify with verifyTenantChain(). Enabling on an existing DB also needs a one-time backfill of historical
# events (the ADR-0030 §3 migration, not yet built) before the chain is complete.
#
# COMMENTED OUT, not `=false`, and the difference used to matter: db/client.ts read this gate with a
# TRUTHINESS test, and the string 'false' is truthy — so an active `=false` line here ARMED the chain on
# every deployment that copied this template, the exact opposite of what the paragraph above promises.
# The read is `=== 'true'` as of ADR-0077 slice 3; leaving the variable unset removes the trap entirely,
# and it is the only gate slice 3 keeps in env (DEFERRED_ENV_GATES — slice 8 owns migrating it).
#
# IF YOUR DEPLOYMENT ALREADY HAS THIS LINE ACTIVE AND SET TO ANYTHING, ITS CHAIN IS RUNNING. Correcting
# the read stops it, and stopping it is NOT self-reporting: verifyTenantChain() only inspects rows that
# carry chain columns, so events appended while the gate is off are absent from the chain rather than a
# break in it, and re-arming later links contiguously across the hole. deploy/deploy.sh therefore runs
# scripts/check-audit-chain-gate.ts before the restart and refuses to continue if the database has a
# chain this env would not keep. Set the value to the literal 'true' to keep it.
# AUDIT_HASH_CHAIN_ENABLED=true

# ── Notification engine (ADR-0034) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The in-app notification centre + task alerts. Off ⇒ dispatch is a no-op and the bell falls back to
# today's computed approvals count (byte-identical).
#
# DOCUMENTED HERE ON PURPOSE (ADR-0077 slice 1), AND DELIBERATELY LEFT COMMENTED. The running
# deployment has it ON via deploy/enable-demo-flags.sh, which is what `LEGACY_ENABLED_MODULE_CODES` in
# packs/catalog.ts backfills an ACTIVE `notifications` entitlement on — and test/module-catalog-drift.ts
# reads BOTH tracked files (`repoShipsFlagOn` is an OR), so the parity ratchet is already satisfied by
# the deploy script alone. Uncommenting this line would ALSO switch the notification centre on for every
# fresh install that copies this file, which is a real behaviour change in a slice that ships none.
# Turn it on per deployment, not by editing the template.
# NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=true

# Movement import XLSX authenticity (server runtime only; legacy CSV needs no key).
# Provision a dedicated random 32-byte base64url key privately; never reuse an identity/vault key.
# Missing or malformed configuration refuses affected workbook endpoints, not the app/build.
# One current key only: changing key or key ID invalidates older workbooks; download again.
# Never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_, embed them in a workbook, or commit a real key.
# MOVEMENT_IMPORT_WORKBOOK_KEY=
# MOVEMENT_IMPORT_WORKBOOK_KEY_ID=

# Optional: tenant whose public login media and browser icon this installation uses.
# First-party auth otherwise uses AUTH_DEFAULT_ORGANIZATION to resolve this tenant.
# Group administrators edit their own presentation in System Configuration → Login & browser appearance.
# LOGIN_PRESENTATION_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Enable only after the ingress overwrites X-Aihr-Request-Source with a verified source IP,
# and the application listener cannot be reached around that ingress. See deploy/internal-auth/README.md.
# Without it, source headers are ignored and legacy authentication global ceilings remain active.
# AIHR_TRUST_REQUEST_SOURCE=1
